course: dictionary
lesson: 11593
title: The top point
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An apex is the very top, or the pointed tip, of something. You can find an apex on a mountain, on a triangle, or on the top of a pyramid. «The hikers reached the apex of the mountain just before sunset.» The clues are reached and the mountain: they had climbed all the way up to the top.
explain: The word apex can also mean the highest point of success. «Her team reached the apex of their season when they won the final.» Here apex does not mean a real top. It means their best moment, the highest they could go.
explain: In science, an apex predator is an animal at the top of a food chain. «Sharks are often called apex predators in the sea.» The word apex tells you this animal is above all the others in the food chain. To check, swap in the meaning: top point. It still makes sense.
fact: An apex is the top or pointed tip of something.
fact: «Apex» can mean the highest point of success, as in «the apex of their career».
fact: In maths, the apex of a cone or pyramid is the point opposite the base.
fact: An «apex predator» is at the top of a food chain.
fact: The plural of apex can be apexes or apices.
exercise: «The hikers reached the apex of the mountain.» What does apex mean here? | The side of the path | The shadow | The bottom | *The very top
exercise: «A pyramid has four triangle sides that meet at its apex.» Where is the apex of the pyramid? | The middle of the base | *The pointed top | The corner of the field | The bottom edge
exercise: In science, an «apex predator» is what? | A plant that grows the fastest | A type of rain cloud | *An animal at the top of a food chain | A small animal hiding in the grass
test: «Her team reached the apex of their season when they won the final.» What does apex mean? | The end of the bus route | The start of the season | *The highest point of success | A sad moment
test: A cone has a round base and a point at the top. What is the point called? | Base | Circle | Rim | *Apex
exam: «The climbers stood at the apex of the hill and looked down at the valley.» What does apex mean? | The bottom of the valley | A stream of water | *The top point | The path to the village
